WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.252
Understanding South Africa's genocide case

00:00:02.252 --> 00:00:05.505
against Israel, part one: some context.

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:07.632
On December 29th, 2023,

00:00:07.632 --> 00:00:08.216
South Africa

00:00:08.216 --> 00:00:09.884
filed an application to begin court

00:00:09.884 --> 00:00:11.678
proceedings against Israel.

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:13.680
They argue that Israel is committing

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.348
genocide against the Palestinian

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:16.766
people in the Gaza Strip.

00:00:16.766 --> 00:00:17.600
I'm going to go into detail

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:18.935
on this document in part three,

00:00:18.935 --> 00:00:19.644
but these allegations

00:00:19.644 --> 00:00:21.438
include killing Palestinians,

00:00:21.438 --> 00:00:22.522
causing them harm

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:24.941
and trying to destroy the Palestinians

00:00:24.941 --> 00:00:25.567
as a group.

00:00:25.567 --> 00:00:26.651
South Africa submitted this

00:00:26.651 --> 00:00:28.528
to the International Court of Justice,

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.113
which was set up in 1945

00:00:30.113 --> 00:00:30.655
to settle disputes

00:00:30.655 --> 00:00:31.948
between nations.

00:00:31.948 --> 00:00:33.867
The final ruling will probably take years

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:34.868
to actually come out,

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:36.411
but the ICJ has come out and ruled

00:00:36.411 --> 00:00:37.746
on a provisional measure,

00:00:37.746 --> 00:00:39.330
ordering Israel to

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:41.207
“take all measures within its power

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:42.459
to prevent...genocide”

00:00:42.459 --> 00:00:43.209
and crucially,

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:45.128
to “ensure the preservation of evidence”

00:00:45.128 --> 00:00:46.755
so they can properly investigate this.

00:00:46.755 --> 00:00:48.131
But they did not order Israel

00:00:48.131 --> 00:00:49.591
to stop military operations

00:00:49.591 --> 00:00:51.134
as South Africa had requested.

00:00:51.134 --> 00:00:51.634
In part two,

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:53.386
I will explain what genocide actually

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:56.514
is per international legal definitions

00:00:56.514 --> 00:00:57.807
so we can learn what that definition

00:00:57.807 --> 00:00:59.309
teaches us about this case.

